Dircctions (Q. 33 and 34) Study $e following information carefully and answerthe questions given below it.A, 4 C, D, E, F and G are playing cards sitting in a circle.(i) F is 2nd to the right of G.(ii) B is neighbour of F but not of E.(iii) E, the neighbour of C, is 4s b the right of G.(iv) D is betvveen E and A.Q.33: Who is tuurth to the left of G?(a) D (b) E (c) c (d) BQ.34: Who is to $e immediate left of G?(a) A (b) C (c) B (d) None of these.Q.35: How many enen numbers are there in the fullowing series of numbers, each of whichis prcceded by an odd number, but not fullowed by an even number?5348971553298735(a) 0 (b) 1 (c) 2 (d) 3
Dircctions (Q.36 and 37) In each of the fullowing questions, affange the wotds ina meaningful, logical older and then select tfte apprcpriate sequence ftom thealternatives given belowforeach of the grcups of vuotds.
Q.36: (1) Mother (2) Child (3) Milk (4) Cry (5) Smile
(a) L,5,2, 4,3 (b) 2, 4, L,3,5 (c) 2, 4,3, L, 5 (d) 3, 2, L,5, 4
Q.37: (1) Vegetable (2) Market (3) Cufring (a) Cooking (5) Food
(a) 1, 2,3, 4,5 (b) 2, L,3, 4, 5 (c) 3, L,2,5, 4 (d) 5, 2, t,3, 4
