Q.15: Quad group of nations consisB of:(a) India, Ausfalia, USA and Japan (b) India, France, Australia and Japan(c) India, Sri Lanka, USA and Japan (d) Australia, USA, Japan and FranceQ.16: In which district of the SbE of lJttarakhand, a disaster caused ht glacier burst hasrecently occuned?(a) Tehri Garhwal (b) Dehradun (c) Chamoli (d) RudraprayagQ.17: In India, Delhi shares its boundary with which of the following states:(a) Punjab only (b) Punjab and Haryana only(c) Punjab, Haryana and Uttar Pradesh only (d) Haryana and Uttar Pradesh onlyQ.18: In India, the Trcpic of Cancer passes through which of the States of North-East ?(a) Assam only (b) Assam and Manipur(c) Assam, Meghalaya and Nagaland (d) Mizoram and Tripura.Q.19: Which of the following statements is nafconect :(a) The President of India is elected by the meffiod of indirect election.(b) A candidate for the Presidenfs office must be at least 45 (furty five) years of age.(c) A candidate fur the Presidenfs office must be qualified to be elected as a member ofLok Sabha(d) President of India can be impeached only for violation of the Constitution of India.Q.20. Under the Constihrtion of India, which provision empowers the Parliament to establishby law a common High Court fur two or more StaEs:(a) Article 324 (b) Article 214 (c) Afticle 231 (d) Article 215Q.21. In a company, 60% workers are males. If the number of female workers in thecompany is 800, what is the number of male workers in the company?(a) 1600 (b) 1400 (c) 1e00 (d) 1200Q.22. A lady going with a boy is asked by a man about the relationship behrueen them. Thewoman replied, "My matemal unde and the unde of his matemal uncle is the same." How isthe lady related to that boy?(a) Grandmother and Grandson (b) Moffier and son(c) Aunt and Nephew (d) None ofthese.Q.23: When we arange the letters of the word 'VRAKIE' in correct order, we get the nameof a river. Fifth letter from left in that name is(a) R (b) E (c) I (d) K
